4. Functional Requirements
Functional requirements describe what the application must do.
4.1 Student module
FR-01: Chat interface

Students should be able to enter questions through a text box and receive responses.

FR-02: FAQ responses

The chatbot should answer questions about:
- Admission procedures
- Courses and departments
- Fee structures
- Examination schedules
- Scholarships
- Library facilities
- Hostel facilities
- Transportation
- Contact information
FR-03: Question matching

The chatbot should recognize questions that have similar meanings or keywords.

For example:
- "How can I apply for admission?"
- "Tell me about the admission process."
- "What is the procedure to join the college?"
These questions should ideally retrieve the same FAQ.

FR-04: Unknown questions

When the chatbot cannot find a sufficiently relevant answer, it should not invent information.

FR-05: Conversation history

Students should be able to see earlier messages during their current conversation.

FR-06: Feedback

Students should be able to indicate whether an answer was helpful.
4.2 Administrator module
FR-07: Administrator login

Only an authorized administrator should be able to manage FAQs.

FR-08: Add FAQs

The administrator should be able to enter a question, answer, category, and relevant keywords.

FR-09: Update FAQs

The administrator should be able to correct outdated information.

FR-10: Delete FAQs

The administrator should be able to remove FAQs that are no longer relevant.

FR-11: View FAQs

The administrator should be able to view all existing FAQs.
