8. Database Design
We will use SQLite because it is lightweight and suitable for this project.

The database will contain three tables.
8.1 FAQ table
Stores questions and their verified answers.
Field	Data type	Purpose
id	INTEGER	Unique FAQ identifier
question	TEXT	Main question
answer	TEXT	Official answer
category	TEXT	Admission, fees, facilities, etc.
keywords	TEXT	Additional matching terms


Example record:
Field	Example
Question	What is the admission process?
Answer	Please refer to the official admissions page for the current admission procedure.
Category	Admissions
Keywords	apply, application, admission, join, eligibility


The example answer is a placeholder. Replace it with verified information from the institution you choose.
8.2 Chat history table
Stores messages for debugging and basic analytics.
Field	Data type	Purpose
id	INTEGER	Unique record identifier
session_id	TEXT	Identifies the browser session
user_message	TEXT	Question asked
bot_response	TEXT	Answer returned
created_at	DATETIME	Time of the interaction


For this student project, we will not require students to create accounts.

Avoid storing unnecessary personal information in chat history.
8.3 Feedback table
Stores student feedback about chatbot responses.
Field	Data type	Purpose
id	INTEGER	Unique feedback identifier
session_id	TEXT	Identifies the chat session
faq_id	INTEGER, nullable	FAQ associated with the response
rating	INTEGER	Helpful or not helpful
created_at	DATETIME	Time of feedback


This information can help identify FAQs that need better answers.
